<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏlyclītus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏlŭ-</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ētus</span></b> ) (ĕ scanned short, Prud.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 269), i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολύκλειτος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated
				Grecian sculptor from Argos or Sicyon</i>, <i>contemporary with Pericles.</i>—Form Polyclitus,
				<i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8, 19</span></i> § 55; <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				18, 70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">86, 296</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or.
				2, 16, 70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 7, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
			103</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 8, 51, 2</span></i>. —Form
			POLYCLETVS, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			3245</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pŏlyclētēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-īus</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>Polycletean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 6, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 2, 2, 67</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
